		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">41</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Write down the count of pairs as 0
2. Read the array numbers
3. Take the first number in the array as current number
4. Take the next number in the array
5. Check if it is same as the current number
6. If yes, increase the count of pairs
7. Repeat steps 4, 5 and 6 until you reach the end of the array
8. Now, Take the second number in the array
9. Repeat steps 4, 5 and 6 until you reach the end of the array
10. Similarly, Repeat steps 8 and 9 until you reach the end of the array
11. By the end, count of pairs will contain the number of good pairs as per problem statement</attribute>
