		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">48</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Until now we have learnt and used various concepts.
- Variables: used to store data
- Arithmetic operators: used for operations like +, -, *, /, %
- Comparison operators: used for operations like &lt;, &lt;=, >, >=, ===, !==
- Conditional statement: used to decide between different actions

But in this problem we want to repeat some set of steps. None of the above concepts can do that.
Loops will help us to repeat a set of steps.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1308.9407333197596</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">3969.491534517428</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">298.9504055812972</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">209.16867892256312</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Until now we have learnt and used various concepts.
- Variables: used to store data
- Arithmetic operators: used for operations like +, -, *, /, %
- Comparison operators: used for operations like &lt;, &lt;=, >, >=, ===, !==
- Conditional statement: used to decide between different actions

But in this problem we want to repeat some set of steps. None of the above concepts can do that.
Loops will help us to repeat a set of steps.</attribute>
